Z||000004||Jncomutt||08-24-2001||02:26 AM||||Well tried lookin in 'search' this was the closest I found.  Still have a few questions.  Ok, I have the entire light assembly that goes in the window.  It has the plug with about 8" of wire to it.  Now do I just splice connect these wires to the brake lights somehow?  Or do I need that other piece mentioned above.  Also, I still have access to the donor car, so what and where is it located so I can grab it off before this car is gone????||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||08-24-2001||08:03 AM||||Go out to your parts car and find the pulg that the 8" piece of wire plugs into. Take it loose from its retainers and remove it to the main harness and cut the wires. It would help you if you can locate the splice in the harness as you need the additional wire.<BR>If you have a Haynes manual it has a wiring schmatice in the back of it. If you don't have one, let us know or try theogres cave. (Link at bottom of page)<P>Hope this helps!<P>What year is your parts car?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||08-24-2001||11:36 AM||||The parts car year is 86.  I'm installing into an 84.  So to get the rest of the wire, I have to take off the entire headliner, and so the interior trim pieces to get there?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||08-24-2001||12:12 PM||||Yes, you got it!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierokid87||08-24-2001||12:35 PM||||All you need is the light the wiring, and the screws/bolt and misc. part that go with it.  Believe it or not all the Fiero from 84-85 had the previsions for the third brake light.  At least the ones Ive see had the holes in the frame.  Its like they planned ahead for that third brake light but never installed it.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fieroguy1987<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
